
## Project Overview
This project performs Exploratory Data Analysis on a cleaned dataset as part of the DecodeLabs internship.

## Objectives
- Calculate mean, median, and count.
- Analyze product-wise order counts and average order values.
- Study monthly order value trends.
- Identify potential outliers using the IQR method.
- Summarize key observations.

## Tools Used
- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

## Key Findings
- Total orders analyzed: 1,200
- Number of product categories: 7
- Mean order value: 1,053.97
- Median order value: 823.62
- Potential outliers: 8
- Missing values: 0
- Duplicate Order IDs: 0

## Conclusion
The analysis revealed differences in product performance, monthly fluctuations in order values, and eight potential high-value outliers. The dataset contained no missing values or duplicate Order IDs.

## Project Output
The Google Colab notebook contains the analysis code, summary statistics, visualizations, and outlier detection results.
